            <ArticleTitle>Nasal symptoms are associated with school performance in adolescents.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>581-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Children with asthma and allergy have higher school absence rates than others, but little is known about their school performance. In a study of 9538 adolescents, nasal symptoms severe enough to affect daily activity were associated with low-grade sum, particularly in adolescents using anti-allergy medication.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
